    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0743" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg593"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I beg to acknowledge,
                    with thanks, the receipt of your personal note of the 13th instant, inclosing a
                    copy of a dispatch from the American minister to Guatemala, in which he reports
                    that a clerk of a Chinese subject having been arrested and assaulted by a
                    Guatemalan policeman, he used his good offices in behalf of the injured man and
                    obtained satisfactory redress, and to request that you will kindly convey to
                    Minister Combs the assurance of my sincere appreciation of his righteous action
                    in this matter.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear Mr. Secretary, very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chentung Liang
                    Cheng.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
